const QUESTION_BANK = [{"id":1,"prompt":["<p>A ball is thrown upward; its height after\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi></semantics></math>\nseconds is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) At what time is the height a maximum? (b) What is the maximum\nheight?</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nseconds. (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nfeet</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PR2"},{"id":2,"prompt":["<p>The cost to produce\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>\nunits is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8500</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) How many units minimize the cost? (b) What is the minimum cost?</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nunits. (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>125</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>125</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>100</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>125</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8500</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>$</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>250</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PR2"},{"id":3,"prompt":["<p>(a) Convert\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>165</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></semantics></math>\nto radians. (b) Convert\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>\nradians to degrees.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>108</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR1"},{"id":4,"prompt":["<p>(a) Convert\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></semantics></math>\nto radians. (b) Convert\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>\nradians to degrees.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>405</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR1"},{"id":5,"prompt":["<p>(a) Find the domain and range of the relation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Does the relation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\ndefine a function? Explain.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Domain:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow></semantics></math>;\nRange:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) No — the input\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nis paired with two different outputs,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>5</mn></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>9</mn></semantics></math>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN1"},{"id":6,"prompt":["<p>Find the domain of each function, in interval\nnotation. (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN3"},{"id":7,"prompt":["<p>A one-to-one function f is given by the table. Find (a) f⁻¹(2),\n(b) f⁻¹(−3), and (c) f⁻¹(6).</p>\n","<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"header\">\n<th><strong>x</strong></th>\n<th><strong>−1</strong></th>\n<th><strong>0</strong></th>\n<th><strong>2</strong></th>\n<th><strong>4</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td>f(x)</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>−3</td>\n<td>−8</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\n(since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>).\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\n(since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>).\n(c)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\n(since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></semantics></math>)</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN6"},{"id":8,"prompt":["<p>Find the inverse formula for (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nand (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN6"},{"id":9,"prompt":["<p>(a) Write in point-slope form the line with slope\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nthrough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Write in slope-intercept form the line through\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF2"},{"id":10,"prompt":["<p>Determine the slope and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi></semantics></math>-intercept\nof the line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\nSlope\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi></semantics></math>-intercept\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF2"},{"id":11,"prompt":["<p>For each function, identify the amplitude,\nperiod, midline, and phase shift. (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>cos</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Amplitude\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn></semantics></math>;\nperiod\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>;\nmidline\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\nphase shift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>\nright. (b) Amplitude\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn></semantics></math>;\nperiod\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></semantics></math>;\nmidline\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\nphase shift\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>\nleft</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PF1"},{"id":12,"prompt":["<p>A sinusoidal wave\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nhas a peak at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nand the next trough at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) Find the amplitude and period. (b) Write the equation.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Amplitude\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PF1"},{"id":13,"prompt":["<p>13. Use the graph of f below. State (a) the domain and range, (b) the interior local minimum and maximum values with their x-locations, and (c) the intervals where f is increasing and decreasing.</p>"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>;\nRange\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Local min\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\nlocal max\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>5</mn></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(c) Decreasing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>;\nincreasing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN3","image":"assets/function-variation-f.png"},{"id":14,"prompt":["<p>14. Use the graph of g below. State (a) the domain and range, (b) the interior local maximum and minimum values with their x-locations, and (c) the intervals where g is increasing and decreasing.</p>"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>;\nRange\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Local max\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>6</mn></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\nlocal min\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(c) Increasing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>;\ndecreasing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN3","image":"assets/function-variation-g.png"},{"id":15,"prompt":["<p>Internet Plan A costs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>$</mi><mn>25</mn></mrow></semantics></math>/month\nplus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>$</mi><mn>0.08</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nper GB of data. Plan B costs a flat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>$</mi><mn>45</mn></mrow></semantics></math>/month.\n(a) Write linear cost models\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>\nGB of data. (b) Find the break-even point by solving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.08</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nGB</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF5"},{"id":16,"prompt":["<p>A candle's height is modeled by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>\nis hours burned. (a) State the slope and describe its meaning in\ncontext. (b) After how many hours will the candle be\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>4</mn></semantics></math>\ninches tall?</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Slope\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></semantics></math>:\nthe candle's height decreases\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn></semantics></math>\ninches per hour. (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nhours</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF5"},{"id":17,"prompt":["<p>(a) Find the exact value of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) The terminal point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nlies on the unit circle corresponding to angle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>θ</mi></semantics></math>.\nFind\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>tan</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>tan</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR5"},{"id":18,"prompt":["<p>(a) Identify the quadrant in which the terminal\nside of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>θ</mi></semantics></math>\nmust lie if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>tan</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) The unit circle shows terminal point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\nFind the reference angle, then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>cos</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Quadrant III. (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>cos</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR5"},{"id":19,"prompt":["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\nFind (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>,\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>,\nand (c)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></semantics></math>.\n(c)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN5"},{"id":20,"prompt":["<p>Use the table to find (a) f(g(1)) and (b) g(f(2)).</p>\n","<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n<col style=\"width: 20%\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"header\">\n<th><strong>x</strong></th>\n<th><strong>1</strong></th>\n<th><strong>2</strong></th>\n<th><strong>3</strong></th>\n<th><strong>4</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td>g(x)</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"even\">\n<td>f(x)</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN5"},{"id":21,"prompt":["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></semantics></math>.\nFind the average rate of change on (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nand (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\nAROC\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\nAROC\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF1"},{"id":22,"prompt":["<p>A cyclist's position in miles along a trail\nafter\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi></semantics></math>\nhours is modeled by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) Find the average rate of change over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></semantics></math>,\nincluding units. (b) Explain what this rate means in the context of the\nride.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi></semantics></math>\nis linear, the average rate of change equals the slope:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>12</mn></semantics></math>\nmi/hr. (b) The cyclist travels at a constant speed of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>12</mn></semantics></math>\nmiles per hour.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF1"},{"id":23,"prompt":["<p>(a) Describe the sequence of transformations\nthat produces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nfrom the parent function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math>.\nWrite the algebraic formula for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nif it is shifted left\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>3</mn></semantics></math>\nunits, vertically stretched by a factor of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn></semantics></math>,\nand shifted up\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>4</mn></semantics></math>\nunits.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Shift left\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>3</mn></semantics></math>,\nreflect across the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>-axis,\nshift down\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>5</mn></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN4"},{"id":24,"prompt":["<p>The parent function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">|</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nhas vertex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>.\nA transformed function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nhas vertex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>,\nopens downward, with the same width as the parent function. (a) Write\nthe coordinate mapping for the vertex. (b) Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>\nin terms of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(c) Write the explicit formula for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(c)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN4"},{"id":25,"prompt":["<p>Find one positive and one negative angle\ncoterminal with (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>170</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></semantics></math>,\nand (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>530</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>190</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR2"},{"id":26,"prompt":["<p>A circular sector has radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\ncm and central angle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>\nradians. (a) Find the exact arc length. (b) Find the exact area.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>\ncm. (b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>100</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>125</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>\ncm<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></msup></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"TR2"},{"id":27,"prompt":["<p>Consider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) Does the parabola open upward or downward? (b) Find the vertex and\nclassify it. (c) State the axis of symmetry, domain, and range.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a) Upward\n(<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></semantics></math>).\n(b) Vertex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>;\nminimum. (c) Axis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>;\ndomain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>;\nrange\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PR1"},{"id":28,"prompt":["<p>Rewrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nin vertex form by completing the square.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"PR1"},{"id":29,"prompt":["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(a) Evaluate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) Find and simplify\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN2"},{"id":30,"prompt":["<p>(a) If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nsolve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b) If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></semantics></math>,\nsolve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> (a)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n(b)\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"FN2"},{"id":31,"prompt":["<p>Find an equation of the line containing the\npoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nwhose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>-intercept\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> Using\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math>.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF2"},{"id":32,"prompt":["<p>Find an equation of the line whose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi></semantics></math>-intercept\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi></semantics></math>-intercept\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>8</mn></semantics></math>.</p>\n"],"answer":"<blockquote>\n<p> Using\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></semantics></math>:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></semantics></math>.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n</blockquote>\n","objective":"LF2"},{"id":33,"prompt":["<p><strong>Name the Graph Transformation</strong></p>\n","<p>Each panel shows a parent function f (dashed) and its transformed\ngraph g (solid). Describe the transformations from f to g, then write an\nequation for g. In A, f(x) = |x|. In B, f(x) = √x.</p>\n"],"answer":"<p> A. Shift right 1, stretch vertically by 2,\nreflect across the x-axis, and shift up 3: g(x) = −2|x − 1| + 3. B.\nShift left 2 and down 1: g(x) = √(x + 2) − 1.</p>\n","objective":"FN4","image":"assets/graph-transformations.png"},{"id":34,"objective":"LF3","prompt":["<p>Use the line shown in the graph. Determine its slope and y-intercept, then write its equation in slope-intercept form.</p>"],"image":"assets/linear-graph.svg","answer":"<p>Slope <strong>m = (−1 − 3)/(2 − 0) = −2</strong>. The y-intercept is <strong>(0, 3)</strong>, so <strong>y = −2x + 3</strong>.</p>"},{"id":35,"objective":"FN1","prompt":["<p>Graph A and Graph B are shown below. Which graph represents a function? Explain using the Vertical Line Test.</p>"],"image":"assets/vertical-line-test.png","answer":"<p><strong>Graph A</strong> represents a function: every vertical line intersects it at most once. Graph B does not: a vertical line through the circle intersects it twice.</p>"},{"id":36,"objective":"LF1","prompt":["<p>The graph shows <math><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math> and a secant line through A(1, 1) and B(4, 2). Find the average rate of change on [1, 4]. Explain what that value tells you about the secant line.</p>"],"image":"assets/secant-square-root.png","answer":"<p>Average rate of change = [g(4) − g(1)]/(4 − 1) = (2 − 1)/3 = <strong>1/3</strong>. This is the slope of the secant line through A and B.</p>"},{"id":37,"objective":"FN4","prompt":["<p>The graph shows the parent function <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math> (dashed) and a transformed graph g (solid). Describe the transformations from f to g, then write g(x) in terms of f and as an explicit formula.</p>"],"image":"assets/horizontal-reflection.png","answer":"<p>Reflect f across the y-axis, then shift it left 2 units. The starting point moves from (0, 0) to (−2, 0). Thus <strong>g(x) = f(−(x + 2)) = √(−x − 2)</strong>, with domain <strong>(−∞, −2]</strong>.</p>"},{"id":38,"objective":"FN5","prompt":["<p>Use the table to evaluate (a) f(g(−2)), (b) g(f(0)), (c) f(g(1)), and (d) g(g(0)). Show the inner lookup first in each case.</p><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">x</th><th scope=\"col\">−2</th><th scope=\"col\">−1</th><th scope=\"col\">0</th><th scope=\"col\">1</th><th scope=\"col\">2</th><th scope=\"col\">3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">f(x)</th><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>−2</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>−1</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">g(x)</th><td>2</td><td>−2</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>−1</td></tr></tbody></table>"],"answer":"<p>(a) g(−2) = 2, so <strong>f(g(−2)) = f(2) = 2</strong>. (b) f(0) = −2, so <strong>g(f(0)) = g(−2) = 2</strong>. (c) g(1) = 3, so <strong>f(g(1)) = f(3) = −1</strong>. (d) g(0) = 1, so <strong>g(g(0)) = g(1) = 3</strong>.</p>"}];
